  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Women-Owned Small Business set-aside obligations totaled $691M in FY2026 to date. The program delivered 2,214 awards with an average award size of $312K. Obligations fell 45.4% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a peak at $1.3B in FY24 and $1.3B in FY25, then a decline to $691M in FY26 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $340M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $81.9M and the Department of Commerce with $59.5M. Other significant buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services with $57M and the Department of Justice with $30.6M. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services lead industries with $127M and $119M respectively. Top vendors include INTELLECT SOLUTIONS, LLC with $18.5M and FCN, INC. with $18.3M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to WOSB set-aside obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The program obligated $691M in FY2026 to date, down 45.4% year over year. Award activity produced 2,214 awards with an average award size of $312K. Fiscal comparisons show obligations were $1.3B in FY24 and $1.3B in FY25 before falling to $691M in FY26 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are WOSB set-aside dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $340M, making it the largest buyer. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $81.9M and the Department of Commerce obligated $59.5M. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services received $127M and $119M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
